        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, Ni(CH3COO)2·4H2O (0.0497 g, 0.2 mmol), Dy(CH3COO)3·xH2O (0.0340 g, 0.1 mmol) and H3L (0.0507 g, 0.2 mmol) were dissolved in 15 mL acetonitrile, followed by addition of triethanolamine (teaH3, 0.0298 g, 0.2 mmol) and NaOH (0.0480 g, 1.2 mmol). The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 50 min, filtered, and the precipitate was dissolved in 5 mL anhydrous methanol. The yellowish-brown methanol solution was placed in a refrigerator for 5 days and then slowly evaporated at room temperature for about 15 days to give yellow-green rod-like crystals suitable for SCXRD. Yield 0.0124 g (about 10.61% based on Dy salt). Elemental analysis indicated that ten lattice CH3OH molecules could be lost during sample collection.",
